meta {
  name: Get String Attribute MaxLength
  type: http
  seq: 10
}

get {
  url: {{CRM_URL}}/EntityDefinitions(LogicalName='{{entityLogicalName}}')/Attributes(LogicalName='{{attributeName}}')/Microsoft.Dynamics.CRM.StringAttributeMetadata?$select=MaxLength
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  $select: MaxLength
}

vars:pre-request {
  entityLogicalName: rpa_onlinesubmission
  attributeName: rpa_onlinesubmissionid
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  Reads MaxLength on a string attribute via the required
  StringAttributeMetadata cast (the base AttributeMetadata type does not
  expose MaxLength directly). Currently targeting rpa_onlinesubmissionid,
  confirmed 20 characters — too short for a 36-character correlationId, the
  finding that reopened blocking decision B2. Reused in place (set
  attributeName in vars:pre-request) to check rpa_uniqueid, which came
  back with the same MaxLength: 20 — see
  plans/duplicate-case-creation-on-timeout-*.md and
  plans/rpa-uniqueid-test-automation-query-field-*.md in fcp-sfd-crm.

  The entity is a variable too, so this works against any entity. To get the
  length of rpa_name on the integration inbound queue, which is
  ApplicationRequired and so must be populated for the write to succeed, set

    entityLogicalName: rpa_integrationinboundqueue
    attributeName:     rpa_name

  and send. Confirmed as MaxLength 100, comfortably more than the 20 that
  rpa_onlinesubmissionid turned out to hold, and enough for a 36-character
  correlation identifier alongside a short prefix.
}
